mcp-grafana is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets AI assistants
work with a Grafana instance and the systems behind it: search and edit
dashboards, query Prometheus, Loki, Tempo and Pyroscope data sources, inspect
alerting rules and incidents, and generate deeplinks.

It runs either as a stdio child of an MCP client or, with -t streamable-http, as
a standalone network service that serves many clients. In service mode each
client can send its own Grafana service account token, and the server can
require a bearer token from callers and serve HTTPS.

The port installs an rc.d script. See pkg-message for the settings.
